OutBound to IPSL
A. Validation Process
    1. 3rd Party/Channel Sends Validation Request to Business Service Engine

    2. Business Service Engine Performs:
        I.  Payload Validation
        II. Perform Boolean - Internal/External Validation required?

    3. Business Service Engine Sends Validation Request to Technical Service Engine

    4. Technical Service Engine Performs:
        I.   Convert to IPSL format
        II.  Send Validation Request (acmt.023) to IPSL
        III. Get Validation Response (acmt.023) from IPSL
        IV.  Convert the Response to Generic Format

    5. Send Validation Response to Business Service Engine from Technical Service Engine

    6. Send Validation Response to 3rd Party/Channel from Business Service Engine

    7. 3rd Party/Channel Process Response

B. Payment Process
    1. 3rd Party/Channel Sends Payment Request to Business Service Engine.

    2. Business Service Engine Performs:
        I.   Payload Validation
        II.  Log Transaction
        III. Get Service Configs
        IV.  Perform Boolean - need Dr/Cr?
            a. If Yes Sends Finacle Request To Dr Target A/c, Cr Pesalink A/c
            b. Receives Finacle Response

    3. Business Service Engine Sends Payment Request (async) to Technical Service Engine
       (It uses async calls for transaction hence callback from kba/IPSL is expected.)

    4. Technical Service Engine Performs:
        I.   Converts Request to IPSL format
        II.  Sends Payment Request (pacs.008) to IPSL
        III. Receives Payment Response
        IV.  Converts the Response to Generic format

    5. Technical Service Engine Sends the Payment Response to Business Service Engine

    6. Business Service Engine Logs the Response

    7. Business Service Engine Sends the Response to the 3rd Party/Channel

    
C. Callback Request From IPSL
    1. IPSL Sends a CallBack Request with Results (pacs.002)

    2. Technical Business Engine Converts the Format to Generic Format

    3. Technical Business Engine Sends the Formatted Request to Business Service Engine

    4. Business Service Engine Processes the CallBack

    5. Business Service Engine Sends a CallBack to the 3rd Party/Channel

    6. 3rd Party/Channel Sends CallBack Response to Business Service Engine

    7. Business Service Engine Sends the Reponse to Technical Service Engine

    8. Technical Service Engine Sends the Response to IPSL


D. (Optional)Status Check - If CallBack doesn't come back
    1. 3rd Party/Channel Initiates a Status Check Request to Business Service Engine

    2. Business Service Engine Sends the Status Check Request (External Check) to Technical Service Engine

    3. Technical Service Engine Converts the Request to IPSL format

    4. Technical Service Engine Sends the Formatted Status Check Request to IPSL

    5. Technical Service Engine Receives Status Check Response fro IPSL

    6. Technical Service Converts the Status Check Response to Generic Format

    7. Technical Service Sends the Status Check Response to Busines Service Engine

    8. Business Service Engine Sends the Status Check Response to the 3rd Party/Channel



    
